  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1: Dry conditions through midweek, with rain \nchances late week.\n\nUpper ridging will quickly build today behind a progressive \ntrough moving into the Atlantic. As a result, strong surface\nhigh pressure will bring dry weather through at least Wednesday.\nRidging will begin to breakdown by Thursday and weak upper\ndisturbances will round the top of the ridge. This will begin \nto introduce a daily chance for scattered afternoon rain/storms \nthrough the weekend. \n\nTemperatures remain elevated throughout the week, with 80s\nacross the mountains and lower 90s east of the mountains.\nOvernight lows still mild...mainly in the low to mid 60s.",
